{"qid":"Q48189","names":["Teutonic Order"],"title":"Teutonic Order","endonym":{"native":"Deutscher Orden","lang":"de"},"capsule":"The Teutonic Order (Deutscher Orden) was a German Catholic military order founded c. 1190 in Acre during the Third Crusade, which pivoted in 1226 to the conversion and conquest of pagan Prussia at the invitation of Duke Conrad of Masovia, establishing a monastic state along the Baltic. Grand Master Winrich von Kniprode (r. 1351–1382) presided over the Order's apex, when it governed Prussia, Livonia, and parts of Estonia from its capital at Marienburg (Malbork). The Order's military power was shattered at the Battle of Grunwald (Tannenberg) in 1410 by a Polish-Lithuanian coalition, and the Second Peace of Toruń (1466) reduced it to a Polish fief; the Prussian branch was secularized as the Duchy of Prussia in 1525 under Grand Master Albert of Brandenburg-Ansbach.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The Teutonic Order's Prussian and Livonian territories are well documented through extensive medieval records; borders evolved through treaties and are reconstructed with good precision for the 14th–15th centuries.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Teutonic Order","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teutonic_Order"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Battle of Grunwald","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Grunwald"}],"britannica":"topic/Teutonic-Order","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Teutonic Order","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Hermann von Salza","nativeName":"Hermann von Salza","roman":"Hermann von Salza","start":1209,"end":1239,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null}